Scraping and Storing Candidate Information,

• Plan: You need to scrape candidate data from reliable sources (like official state/national election commission websites). Implement functionality to filter this data based on the location (e.g., zip code, state, or region) and election type (governor, city council, etc.) dynamically.

• Implementation Recommendations:

• Data Scraping: Use libraries like BeautifulSoup or Scrapy to collect information about candidates from the election commission websites.
• Data Storage:

• Store scraped data in a collection-oriented database like MongoDB for unstructured data (or PostgreSQL if you need relational organization).

• Structure database tables or collections with fields: candidate_name, election_type, region, and specifics.

• Scoping by User’s Region:

• Implement logic to capture and filter user-specific data (e.g., region, zip code, or district). For regional filters, you might map user locations using Google Places API or similar APIs.


Displaying Relevant Candidates,

• Implement backend logic to dynamically query and serve filtered candidates based on:

• User-specific location (region/state).

• Current election cycle and type.

• Frontend Integration:

• Develop a UI that displays candidate profiles dynamically.

• Use modern JavaScript frameworks (e.g., React, Vue, or similar) to make the data interactive.

• Include details like:

• Candidate Bio.

• Political Party.

• Key Agendas.

• Voting history, etc.


Notifications About Elections,

• Implement notifications using CRON jobs or scheduled tasks with real-time capabilities.

• Steps:

• Identify key election events and their timelines (e.g., early voting, registration deadlines).

• Store these events in the database with triggers based on the user’s location.

• Notify users:

• Use Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) or OneSignal/APNs for push notifications.

• Use Twilio or SendGrid for SMS/Email notifications.

• Notifications for:
• Upcoming early voting periods.
• Specific milestones about primaries/general elections.
• Upcoming Enhancements: Use Progressive Web App (PWA) technology to display native-like push notifications.
